 22. Checkpoints
@@ -791,6 +806,19 @@ Recover
 
 Blind retry could produce a duplicate payment.
 
+For a consequential corrective transition, a parent World-version mismatch
+MUST reject the stale commit attempt. A VerificationReceipt bound to the old
+parent becomes inapplicable to a new candidate. Retry or merge MUST prepare a
+new candidate against the current parent, obtain fresh verification, and
+revalidate authorization where the applicable policy requires it. Historical
+verification records MUST NOT be erased.
+
+Recovery MUST preserve the stable action/idempotency identity and reconcile
+against available external-authority observations and evidence before any
+retry that could duplicate an effect. UNKNOWN remains UNKNOWN until evidence
+resolves it, and Veda MUST NOT claim exactly-once external execution without
+an explicit external-system guarantee.
+
