+These recovery events are pre-commit factual records unless they reference a
+successful World commit. Event persistence, RecoveryVerified,
+RecoveryCompleted, RecoveryReceipt and Chronicle projection MUST NOT
+independently confer World commit authority.
+
+Only the World Kernel may perform the authoritative CAS commit. That one
+boundary MUST atomically expose all three, or none:
+
+1. the resulting authoritative World version;
+2. the immutable WORLD_COMMIT_RECEIPT; and
+3. the durable committed-event delivery intent.
+
+The delivery intent is created inside the same boundary and successful
+modeled-World outcome delivery occurs afterward. Failed, partial, UNKNOWN or
+indeterminate recovery MUST NOT emit a successful modeled-World outcome.
