+RecoveryReceipt is a Veda-owned recovery evidence and summary record. It is
+not a VerificationReceipt or a WORLD_COMMIT_RECEIPT, cannot independently
+authorize or prove authoritative modeled-World commitment, and cannot prove
+that an external effect was undone. The linkage fields preserve the exact
+parent World version, candidate transition hash, identified evidence set and
+verification policy version for a consequential corrective transition. A
+VerificationReceipt reference MAY be added only when that record exists; a
+WORLD_COMMIT_RECEIPT reference MAY be added only after a successful World
+Kernel commit. Recovery evidence may exist before verification, and absent
+references MUST remain absent rather than invented.
+
+For a consequential corrective transition, `evidence[]` represents the
+complete identified evidence set available for that recovery attempt. An
+irreversible external effect cannot be transactionally erased by rewriting
+Veda's modeled World State; any compensation is a separately authorized,
+observable and verifiable corrective action.
+
+Failed, rejected, partial, UNKNOWN, indeterminate, stale and
+recovery-required attempts MUST retain truthful durable factual evidence linked
+to the stable attempted action/recovery identity. The recovery result MUST
+distinguish external execution status, observed external effect, verification
+status, World commit status and recovery-required or escalation status. A
+successful external compensation MAY be recorded as an external fact even
+when modeled-World commit has not succeeded; it MUST NOT be represented as a
+successful modeled-World outcome.
+
